PART A -- the mimetic constraint is an IDENTITY, not an equation
==========================================================================
  [PASS] A1 [THE IDENTITY] with g = -(g~^{ab} d_a T d_b T) g~, the constraint
      g^{mu nu} d_mu T d_nu T = -1 holds IDENTICALLY (sympy, 1+1, general A,B)
         measured: g^(mu nu) d_mu T d_nu T = -1
         This is the whole point of mimetic gravity: the constraint is not an
         equation of motion restricting the fields; it is a DEFINITION of
         the physical metric. No dynamics is spent enforcing it.

